Next, we add row and column totals to convert these results into a full contingency table:

::: {#a81bb2dd .cell execution_count=6}
``` {.python .cell-code}
contigency_table = (contingency_df
 .rename(dict(Completed='Yes', Not_Completed='No'))
 .vstack(pl.DataFrame({
     'Variant':'Total',
     'Yes': contingency_df.select(pl.sum('Completed')),
     'No': contingency_df.select(pl.sum('Not_Completed')),
     }))
 .with_columns(Total=pl.sum_horizontal(pl.nth(1,2)))
 )
contigency_table
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=6}
